  "notes": "From horror-25.jpg (item 054). Nearest mode: cauliflower_scales, whose lit bands and domed bubble cells are horror's scales; lace_holes, the prompt's guess, draws a glowing web with lit holes and no relief. What this adds over the entry (horror_scales in cauliflower_scales): molten_flow's three viewed sheets as translucent folds laid before the lights, masked by the set's distance so they stay off the lace (unmasked, at a lace-dense seat the views' bands alias into a pale wash over the finer scales), and red veins: the stripe average's crests masked to the set and a red de hairline. A far-field multiply to black was tried and dropped: sinking the ground makes the tone pass (median 0.092) lift everything else, and the lace went bone white. Seats are a plain gallery scout with --min-ink 0.15 (seed 54): the reference is textured edge to edge. No engine change. Lesson: a `view` is one more escape loop over the whole frame, and a turned or zoomed-out view of a deep seat can land on interior points, each iterated to the seat's `maxiter`: a three-view stack at a phoenix seat with `maxiter` 14,428 drew nothing in 13 minutes where the same seat without views took under a minute. Draw a view-heavy stack's formulations at seats of low `maxiter` (a few thousand) and time one draft before a batch. Explorer cost (080, `style cost`, read beside other Node workers: an upper bound): 215 s as WebAssembly on one thread at 1280x800 ss2 at its deepest kept seat (phoenix-classic_9a93355d, maxiter 1,071), under the 5-minute bar.",
